 crime, poor laws, democracy, universal suffrage, education, reformation of criminals in the state of New York, with a proposition to provide for the surplus working population of England, plan and estimate:- to which is added, suggestions for upholding the property of the church, preserving vested rights, exonerating dissenters from contributing thereto, and applying the tythes for the support of the poor". --  Handwritten inscriptions on front-cover: "[?] Buchanan's letter, 26 August '37 (private letters)" and "Poor law question page 48. Estimate - 75". -- Includes table of contents end of volume.</dc:description><dc:identifier>http://opac.oireachtas.ie/Data/Library3/Library3/DCT127004.pdf</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>New York Printed by William A. Mercein</dc:publisher><dc:language>en</dc:language><dc:source>The Oireachtas Library &amp; Research Service</dc:source><dc:subject>Criminals -- Rehabilitation -- Great Britain -- History -- 19th century.</dc:subject><dc:subject>Prisons -- United States -- 19th century.</dc:subject><dc:subject>Prisons -- Great Britain -- 19th century.</dc:subject><dc:subject>Poverty.</dc:subject><dc:subject>Poor laws -- Great Britain -- History -- 19th century.</dc:subject><dc:title>Facts and observations in relation to the extension of state prisons in England, also bearing on poverty and crime Pamphlets</dc:title><dc:type>InteractiveResource</dc:type><dc:type>Software</dc:type><dc:type>software, multimedia</dc:type><dcterms:spatial>New York</dcterms:spatial><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/15416/Data_Library3_Library3_DCT127004_pdf"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/15416/Data_Library3_Library3_DCT127004_pdf"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/europeana/15416/Data_Library3_Library3_DCT127004_pdf"><dc:date rdf:resource="#1834"></dc:date><edm:europeanaProxy>true</edm:europe